 "tags": [
  {
   "description": "Bounded simulator subset of the official AWS Lake Formation API (2017-03-31). Every other official operation returns HTTP 501 UnknownOperationException. LF-tags, LF-tag expressions, the Regional data lake settings and registered Amazon S3 locations are stored records, and Lake Formation permissions are not evaluated: GrantPermissions, RevokePermissions, ListPermissions, LF-tag assignment to resources, data cells filters, opt-ins, transactions, query planning, temporary credentials and every other official operation return UnknownOperationException with HTTP 501. Data lake administrators, default permissions and tags therefore change what no principal may do. An LF-tag holds 1 to 50 values that cannot change after creation: UpdateLFTag is not implemented because the stored model cannot apply TagValuesToAdd and TagValuesToDelete to the values already held, so a tag is deleted and created again to change them. An LF-tag expression is stored without checking that the LF-tags it names exist, and ListLFTags does not support the ResourceShareType filter because no tag is shared. LF-tags and expressions have no ARN in AWS: the ARN used for authorization is a simulator form. A duplicate LF-tag or expression fails with InvalidInputException (HTTP 400) because the official operations model no already-exists exception, and the missing-resource and already-registered failures use the modeled EntityNotFoundException and AlreadyExistsException. Data lake settings start as AWS documents them for an account that never changed them: no administrators and IAM_ALLOWED_PRINCIPALS holding ALL on new databases and tables. PutDataLakeSettings replaces the whole document, accepts at most 30 administrators and 30 read-only administrators, and stores everything else without resolving principals. RegisterResource stores an Amazon S3 location and its IAM role without reading the location or assuming the role: ResourceArn must be an Amazon S3 ARN, and either RoleArn or UseServiceLinkedRole true must be given, the latter being stored as the Lake Formation service-linked role ARN. WithFederation, HybridAccessEnabled and WithPrivilegedAccess are stored as flags with no effect, and registering a location nested inside or around a registered one is allowed although AWS refuses it. CatalogId, when sent, must be the simulator account. The limits of 1000 LF-tags, 1000 expressions and 100 registered locations per Region are local.",
   "name": "AWS Lake Formation"
  }
 ],
